mode: "100644"
text: "# Examples — GEO in practice\n\nWorked examples showing the audit → levers → measurement flow, plus honest scope. Subject: a solo\nfounder building a SaaS social scheduler. Voice context is the blunt indie-founder voice; your output\nuses the loaded `voice.md`, `brand-profile.md`, `audience.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Example 1 — the audit (always start here)\n\n**Queries (buyer-intent + fan-out):** \"best social media scheduler for solopreneurs,\" \"free social\nscheduler,\" \"[competitor] alternative,\" \"how to schedule a week of posts.\"\n**Run across** ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini (incognito). **Findings (illustrative — from an actual run,\nnot invented):** competitor named in 3/4; you're absent; **cited sources** = a Reddit r/socialmedia\nthread, a \"7 best schedulers 2026\" listicle, and a YouTube review. Perplexity leaned on Reddit.\n**Read-out:** the citation sources *are* the to-do list → get authentically into that Reddit\nconversation, earn listicle inclusion, get a YouTube review. Re-run monthly.\n\n## Example 2 — the Reddit play (authentic)\n\nThe audit shows Perplexity citing Reddit. **Play:** the founder genuinely participates in the\nbuyer-intent threads (\"what scheduler do you use?\") with specific, helpful, experience-based answers —\ndisclosing they built one where relevant, not spamming. Over time those threads (and the brand\nmention in them) become citable. **Not:** ten sockpuppets posting \"try [product]!\" — that's\nastroturfing (detectable, removed, trust-destroying).\n\n## Example 3 — the YouTube play\n\nBrand mentions in **video titles + transcripts** are a top AI-Overview correlate. **Play:** publish a\nvideo titled \"How to Schedule a Week of Social Posts in 20 Minutes (Free)\" — say the brand + the\ncategory keywords in the script (transcript), caption it. Now it can surface in AI Overviews *and* in\nYouTube/Google search. → `reels-script`, `social-seo`, `tiktok-growth`.\n\n## Example 4 — making a page extractable (before → after)\n\n**Before:** a meandering blog post, no headers, the answer buried in paragraph 6.\n**After:** opens with a **one-sentence TL;DR answer**, **question-shaped H2s** (\"How much does it cost?\n\", \"Is there a free plan?\"), a **comparison table**, two **verifiable stats with sources**, a quotable\nline, **FAQ schema**, and a **named author + update date.** Same facts — now liftable into an answer.\n\n## Example 5 — entity clarity\n\nThe model describes the brand vaguely/wrongly in the audit. **Fix:** make the **one-line description**\nidentical across the site, social bios, and listings (\"the social scheduler for solo founders who hate\nscheduling\"); claim listings; ensure consistent naming. Now the model has a clean entity to recommend\nfor the category.\n\n---\n\n## Honest scope (say this)\n\n- **Probabilistic, not guaranteed** — you influence the odds of being cited; engines change and\n  citations decay.\n- **No invented numbers** — no made-up \"share of voice\" or citation %; run the audit / a tool.\n- **No astroturfing** — authentic mentions and real reviews only; fakes are detectable and backfire.\n- **Earned > owned** — most citations aren't your pages; invest in community/earned mentions.\n- **Spans the web too** — the full discipline includes your site/blog structure + schema, broader than\n  social; pair with `social-seo` for the retrieval foundation.\n- **No WoopSocial analytics** — measure via the manual audit + GEO tools + AI referral traffic.\n\n---\n\n## What the examples share\n\n- They **start with the audit** (real findings, not guesses) and let the **cited sources set the\n  strategy.**\n- They lead with **earned/community mentions** (Reddit/YouTube/listicles) where AI actually looks.\n- They make content **extractable** and the **entity** clear.\n- They stay **authentic** and **honest about measurement**.\n"
